        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/alamosa/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded by the Denver and Rio Grande Railroad, Alamosa quickly became a vital rail hub with extensive repair and shipping facilities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamosa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Adams State University, established in 1921 as a teachers college, now offers undergraduate and graduate programs in education, business, and the arts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamosa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On July 10, 2020, Alamosa shattered weather records by dropping 37°F and then soaring to 92°F within twelve hours.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamosa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every June, Alamosa hosts “Summer Fest on the Rio,” a weekend celebration featuring music, food, and river activities.",
